course: dictionary
lesson: 9467
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning a little depending on where they are used. Starve is one of them. Its main meaning is to suffer, or even die, because you have no food for a long time. «Plants and animals starve when they have no food» is the kind of science sentence you may meet in class.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is needed. «I'm starving» said before lunch is not usually a real emergency. It is an everyday way to say «I'm very hungry», a big, exaggerated way of talking. Ask yourself: is someone really in danger, or are they just hungry?
explain: Starve can also mean to not give food to someone, or to be starved of something you need. A plant kept in a dark cupboard is starved of light, so it grows pale and weak. The word stays the same; only the thing that is missing changes.
fact: Starve has the forms starve, starves, starved and starving.
fact: To starve is to suffer or die because you have no food for a long time.
fact: «Starved of» means not getting enough of something you need, such as «starved of light» or «starved of water».
fact: «I'm starving» is an everyday way to say «I'm very hungry», and it is usually not a real emergency.
fact: The old saying «feed a cold, starve a fever» is a myth: the body needs drinks and energy when you are ill.
exercise: «Plants and animals without food will starve.» What does starve mean here? | Sleep through the whole day | Shout loudly for help | *Suffer or die because there is no food for a long time | Grow very tall and green
exercise: Ella says «I'm starving» at two o'clock, three hours after a full school lunch. What does she really mean? | She has been starved of sleep | She is in real danger and needs help now | She has not had any food at all today | *I'm quite hungry, and I am exaggerating a little
exercise: «The plant in the dark cupboard was starved of light.» What does starved of light mean? | It was painted bright yellow | *It did not get enough light, which it needs | It was very large and heavy | It was watered every day
test: «Her plants were starved of water all summer.» What does starved of water mean? | They were given far too much water | *They did not get enough water | They were painted blue | They were planted in a big pot
test: Which meaning of starve is used in «I'm starving» said after a big lunch? | To be starved of attention | To suffer or die with no food at all | To refuse someone food on purpose | *An everyday way of saying I'm hungry
exam: Which sentence uses starve to mean suffer or die because there is no food for a long time? | *Wild animals may starve in a long, cold winter if they cannot find food | «I'm starving» before lunch is an exaggeration | The garden was starved of rain all week | The old saying «feed a cold, starve a fever» is a myth
